| ^ ## APAC total    |      |       |        | = [Q1_Web; block].sum() | = [Q1_Shop; block].sum() | = [Q1_Sum; block].sum()                  |        | = [Q2_Web; block].sum() | = [Q2_Shop; block].sum() | = [Q2_Sum; block].sum()                  | = [H1_Sum; block].sum()                 |       |        | = [Q3_Web; block].sum() | = [Q3_Shop; block].sum() | = [Q3_Sum; block].sum()                  |        | = [Q4_Web; block].sum() | = [Q4_Shop; block].sum() | = [Q4_Sum; block].sum()                  | = [H2_Sum; block].sum()                 | = [FY_Sum; block].sum()                 |
| ^ # World total    |      |       |        | = [Q1_Web; block].sum() | = [Q1_Shop; block].sum() | = [Q1_Sum; block].sum()                  |        | = [Q2_Web; block].sum() | = [Q2_Shop; block].sum() | = [Q2_Sum; block].sum()                  | = [H1_Sum; block].sum()                 |       |        | = [Q3_Web; block].sum() | = [Q3_Shop; block].sum() | = [Q3_Sum; block].sum()                  |        | = [Q4_Web; block].sum() | = [Q4_Shop; block].sum() | = [Q4_Sum; block].sum()                  | = [H2_Sum; block].sum()                 | = [FY_Sum; block].sum()                 |

sheet Check

| Label         | Value                                       |
| ------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| Grand total   | = Sales[FY_Sum; 21]                     |
| Regions added | = Sales[FY_Sum; 10] + Sales[FY_Sum; 20] |
| Halves added  | = Sales[H1_Sum; 21] + Sales[H2_Sum; 21] |

// A subtotal, a local total and a regional total are summary rows, `^`,
// under what they sum, and several may close one block: a sum, a mean and
// a maximum. `block` is the rows under a head, up to the end of its block,
// with no heading of their own, so no row is counted twice.
sheet Costs

| Place            | Net                    |
| ---------------- | ---------------------- |
| # World          |                        |
| ## EMEA          |                        |
| ### UK           |                        |
| London           | 10                     |
| Leeds            | 5                      |
| ^ ### UK sum     | = [Net; block].sum()   |
| ^ ### UK mean    | = [Net; block].mean()  |
| ### France       |                        |
| Paris            | 7                      |
| Lyon             | 9                      |
| ^ ### France sum | = [Net; block].sum()   |
| ^ ## EMEA sum    | = [Net; block].sum()   |
| ^ ## EMEA max    | = [Net; block].max()   |
| ## APAC          |                        |
| Tokyo            | 20                     |
| ^ ## APAC sum    | = [Net; block].sum()   |
| ^ # World sum    | = [Net; block].sum()   |

// `rollup` is `group_by` laid out as blocks, for a query to give its
// result the shape written by hand above: a head row for each group of the
// outer keys, the groups inside it, and a summary row of the same
// aggregates at its foot. It is read-only, and folds in the app like the
// sheets above, the head of a closed block showing its summary.
sheet Revenue

| Region | Country | City     | Sales | Orders |
| ------ | ------- | -------- | ----- | ------ |
| EMEA   | UK      | London   | 120   | 14     |
| EMEA   | UK      | Leeds    | 45    | 6      |
| EMEA   | France  | Paris    | 98    | 11     |
| EMEA   | France  | Lyon     | 52    | 7      |
| APAC   | Japan   | Tokyo    | 140   | 16     |
| APAC   | Japan   | Osaka    | 61    | 8      |
| APAC   | India   | Delhi    | 77    | 9      |
| APAC   | India   | Mumbai   | 83    | 10     |

sheet ByPlace := Revenue |> rollup(Region, Country, City) |> agg(Sales.sum(), Orders.sum())

// Long text at the edge of a column. Each column is 14 characters wide, the
// length of its `---`. Nothing said, a text spills over the empty cells to
// its right; `String[clip]` cuts it off at the column's edge and
// `String[wrap]` carries it on to more lines. The style bar's ⇢ menu sets
// them, for text columns only.
sheet Texty

Clip : String[clip]
Wrap : String[wrap]

| Spill                                   | Clip                                                    | Wrap                                       | Kind                        |
| --------------                          | --------------                                          | --------------                             | ----                        |
| Spills over the empty cells beside it   |                                                         |                                            | spill                       |
| A long note, cut short by the next cell | "Clipped at the column's edge, \n    never shown whole" | Wrapped on to more lines inside the column | all three                   |
| Short                                   | Short                                                   | Short                                      | fits                        |
| "Some text\nwith a newline"             | "Some text\nwith a newline"                             | "Some text\nwith a newline"                | "some text\nwith a newline" |
